>>
endobj
586 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (IT support requests in many organisations are raised through telephone calls, e-mails and informal messages, which makes them difficult to categorise, prioritise, assign and follow up. Requests can be lost or duplicated, users do not know who is working on their problem, and the support team has no consolidated view of open tickets, resolved tickets or the workload of each agent. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
587 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (This project presents IT SERVICE DESK MANAGEMENT SYSTEM, A It ticket support system developed on the Zoho Creator low-code platform. The application is built around five forms: Users, Support Agents, Categories, Tickets and Ticket Comments. A user submits a ticket with a title, description, category, priority and an optional attachment; an administrator assigns it to a support agent; and the agent moves it through the statuses Open, In Progress, Resolved and Closed while adding comments. The creation date and the resolution date are recorded for every ticket. Reports are provided for tickets, agents, categories and users, and a dashboard presents key performance indicators and charts for ticket status, priority, category and agent workload. Role-based access separates Users, Support Agents and Admins wherever the platform supports it, and short Deluge scripts validate ticket data. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 473 0 R
/E (Functional test cases are defined for form validation, ticket submission and assignment, status tracking, comments, reports and role-based access, and a format for recording user acceptance feedback is provided. The project shows that a maintainable, browser- based and mobile-accessible helpdesk can be obtained without building a conventional web application, giving every request a traceable record from submission to resolution. E-mail notification, service-level timers and integrations with external tools are identified as future enhancements and are outside the scope of this version. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
