/E (IT support function that receives problems from its users and resolves them. Typical requests concern hardware faults, software installation, network connectivity, account and login problems, e-mail, printers and other issues. Each request must be recorded, classified, given a priority, assigned to a suitable support agent, followed until it is resolved, and closed with a record of when it was raised and when it was resolved. This discipline is part of IT service management, for which the ITIL framework describes the service desk and incident-handling practices [8]. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
