1496 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 497 0 R
/E (Figure 4.3 shows the ticket life cycle. A user submits a ticket on the Tickets form; it is saved with the status Open and the creation date. The Admin assigns it to a support agent, who changes the status to In Progress and adds comments; the script DS-03 refuses a comment on a Closed ticket. When the status is changed to Resolved or Closed, the validation script DS-01 checks the dates and cancels the submission with an alert if they are inconsistent, and DS-02 stamps the resolution date. The user and the agent can then read the outcome and the comments on the ticket. )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
