<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 506 0 R
/T (All three workflows are form workflows, because the automation is triggered by saving a record. The ticket status is changed by the support agent and no approval process is used. A scheduled workflow \(for example, a reminder for tickets that stay Open\), an approval process and a Blueprint that enforces the order of the statuses were considered unnecessary for the first version and are listed as future enhancements. )
/E (All three workflows are form workflows, because the automation is triggered by saving a record. The ticket status is changed by the support agent and no approval process is used. A scheduled workflow \(for example, a reminder for tickets that stay Open\), an approval process and a Blueprint that enforces the order of the statuses were considered unnecessary for the first version and are listed as future enhancements. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1677 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 506 0 R
/T (DS-01 runs when a ticket is added or edited. It blocks a resolution date that is earlier than the creation date and blocks a Resolved or Closed ticket that has no assigned agent. Each check displays an alert and cancels the submission, so the inconsistent record is never stored. )
/E (DS-01 runs when a ticket is added or edited. It blocks a resolution date that is earlier than the creation date and blocks a Resolved or Closed ticket that has no assigned agent. Each check displays an alert and cancels the submission, so the inconsistent record is never stored. )
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [10]
>>
